  "title": "Culturally Grounded Personas in Large Language Models: Characterization and Alignment with Socio-Psychological Value Frameworks",
  "summary": "This study investigates how large language models (LLMs) can generate culturally grounded personas, which are defined as representations of people in society that reflect stable cultural values and moral frameworks. The research explores how these personas align with frameworks like the World Values Survey and Moral Foundations Theory, aiming to better understand their alignment with socio-psycho-cultural dimensions.",
